    "answer": {
      "short": "$250$.\n\nThe eight-term and ten-term sums have the same average term.",
      "worked": "The eight terms from $a_2$ to $a_9$ have average $\\dfrac{200}{8}=25$. Since $a_2=a_1+d$ and $a_9=a_{10}-d$, their endpoint sum equals $a_1+a_{10}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{a_2+a_9}{2}&=\\frac{200}{8}\\\\\n\\frac{a_1+a_{10}}{2}&=25\\\\\na_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_9+a_{10}&=10\\left(\\frac{a_1+a_{10}}{2}\\right)\\\\\na_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_9+a_{10}&=10\\times25\\\\\na_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_9+a_{10}&=250.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
